{
  "__comment__": "Hardware-free setup for the SimplePointScan panel (scan.scanWidgetType \"SimplePointScan\"): overview and acquisition point scanning on the Advanced scan path. Two APDs (counter-input detectors) and three gated lasers on a SIMULATED NIDAQ (nidaq.simulation = true), so overview, region, pixel size, dwell and laser channels can be tried with NO real hardware. X/Y are galvo-like smooth axes with the example_sted limits (vel_max 0.1 um/us, acc_max 1e-4 um/us^2, 1.75 um/V over +-10 V, so a 35 um field); Z is a piezo-like STEPPED axis. scan.simplePointScan gives the objective NA the pixel slider's Nyquist end is computed from.",
